WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.190
Overprotective parenting is common in many Chinese families.
过度保护式育儿在许多中国家庭中很常见。

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:21.410
Parents of this kind arrange every detail of their children’s lives, from what to eat and wear to which university and major to choose, and they rarely let their children try anything new for fear that they might make mistakes or get hurt.
这类父母安排孩子生活中的每一个细节，从吃什么、穿什么，到选哪所大学、读什么专业，而且他们很少让孩子尝试任何新事物，生怕孩子会犯错或受伤。

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.430
Although such behavior comes from love, it often does more harm than good.
这种行为虽然出于爱，却往往弊大于利。

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:35.670
Children who have never made their own decisions may lack independence and confidence, and they may feel lost when they leave home for college or work.
从未自己做过决定的孩子可能缺乏独立性和自信心，离家去上大学或工作时，他们可能会感到无所适从。

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:40.190
Moreover, mistakes and setbacks are an important part of growing up.
此外，错误和挫折是成长的重要组成部分。

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:47.690
By shielding children from every risk, parents deprive them of the chance to learn from failure and become resilient.
父母让孩子避开每一种风险，也就剥夺了他们从失败中学习、变得坚强的机会。

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:55.540
To address this issue, parents should first change their mindset and realize that letting go is also a form of love.
为了解决这个问题，父母首先应当转变观念，明白放手也是一种爱。

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:06.830
They can begin by giving children age-appropriate responsibilities, such as doing chores or managing their pocket money, and allowing them to make choices and bear the consequences.
他们可以先给孩子分配适合其年龄的责任，比如做家务或管理零花钱，并允许他们自己做选择、承担后果。

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:15.800
Schools and communities can also help by offering parenting courses and organizing activities that encourage children to explore on their own.
学校和社区也可以提供帮助，开设育儿课程，组织鼓励孩子自主探索的活动。

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:20.340
In this way, children will be better prepared for adult life.
这样，孩子就能为成年生活做好更充分的准备。
